</year>, <volume>37</volume>, 479&#x02013;489.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18224258</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ref15"><note id="cit15"><p>Lsac is the ratio at which assembled to disassembled species is 1:1</p></note><mixed-citation id="cit15a" publication-type="journal"><label>a</label><name><surname>Ercolani</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name> <source>J. Phys. Chem. B</source> <year>1998</year>, <volume>102</volume>, 5699&#x02013;5703.</mixed-citation><mixed-citation id="cit15b" publication-type="journal"><label>b</label><name><surname>Chi</surname><given-names>X.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Guerin</surname><given-names>A. J.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Haycoc</surname><given-names>R. A.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Hunter</surname><given-names>C. A.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Sarson</surname><given-names>L. D.</given-names></name> <source>J. Chem. Soc., Chem. Commun.</source> <year>1995</year>, 2563&#x02013;2565.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ref16"><mixed-citation id="cit16" publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Ercolani</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name> <source>J. Am. Chem. Soc.</source> <year>2003</year>, <volume>125</volume>, 16097&#x02013;16103.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14678002</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ref17"><mixed-citation id="cit17" publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Weiss</surname><given-names>J. N</given-names></name> <source>FASEB J.</source> <year>1997</year>, <volume>11</volume>, 835&#x02013;841.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9285481</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="ref18"><note id="cit18"><p>The head of the tetrad is defined as the side in which rotation following the direction of the N1H&#x02019;s is clockwise. See <xref rid="si1" ref-type="notes">Figure S18</xref> for more information</p></note><mixed-citation id="cit18a" publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>F. W.</given-names></name>; <name><surname>Lau</surname><gi